The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md, but it didn't get committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the git add was refused and the harness's || true skipped the commit. The file is still on disk for the planner.

Found this session:
• New bug, filed as #1072. /doctor reports the git branch wrong in two cases:
  • In a fresh git init repo with no commits, which is on master, it says branch: detached.
  • When HEAD really is detached, it says branch: HEAD.
  
  The shared helper git::git_branch() uses git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD, which fails on a branch with no commits and returns the literal HEAD when detached. It has 10 callers, plus a sibling in context.rs that feeds the branch line of the system prompt. I only ran /doctor; the other callers are read from code. Claude Code 2.1.309 fixed a bug of the same kind the day before ("showing HEAD as the branch").
• Build and runs: the harness reported the build green at session start, and CI is green on the current commit. The last 10 sessions completed 2/2 tasks each, with 0 reverts. The one cancelled evolve run, last night at 20:43, has no job records. I'm guessing a concurrency cancel, not a failure, but didn't check. yoyo -p returned PONG, and yoyo status zz exits 2 as intended.
• Smaller friction: yoyo config get model says "using default" but doesn't say which model that is.
• Rival research: Claude Code 2.1.309 now loads only the start of an oversized CLAUDE.md; we have the same gap in #1070. Codex 0.164 masks credentials in Bash commands, which is the area of #1064. Codex 0.163 lets you steer a reply mid-turn; I haven't checked whether yoyo can. I saved these to yopedia as a dated changelog comparison note.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. #1072. It sits outside main, which the trajectory flagged for taking 3 of the last 5 self-driven diffs.
2. The /bg command, the last door still open on #1063.
3. Either the #1064 default, split by which commands need the key (@yuanhao handed that decision back to us), or #1070.
